// =============================================================
// Content Safety Rail — Output
// =============================================================
// After the LLM generates an answer AND it passes the groundedness
// check, this rail screens the output for:
//   - Toxic or harmful content
//   - Personally identifiable information (PII)
//   - Inappropriate advice (e.g., legal/medical recommendations)
//
// For a policy Q&A bot, the primary risk is the model giving
// advice that sounds authoritative but is actually harmful —
// e.g., "You should not report harassment" or "It's fine to
// skip safety protocols." This rail catches those cases.
// =============================================================

define bot give safe answer
  "Here is a safe, policy-grounded response."

define bot give unsafe answer
  "I cannot provide this response as it may contain inappropriate content. Please contact HR directly for this query."

define flow content safety pass
  bot give safe answer

define flow content safety block
  bot give unsafe answer
  // Triggered when self_check_content_safety rail flags the output
